<BaseLayout title="Limeade · Nizam Mohammed" description="Limeade, a real-time computer vision system for scooter rider safety, built at DemonHacks with YOLOv8 hazard detection and an LLM reasoning layer." headerVariant="internal" activeNav="work">
<article class="project"><a href="/work" class="project__back project__back--top">← Work</a><header class="project__hero"><div class="project__hero-media project__hero-media--shot"><a class="pshot pshot--link" href="https://github.com/Nizamohammed/Limeade" target="_blank" rel="noopener" aria-label="View the Limeade code on GitHub"><img src="/project/limeade.jpg" alt="Limeade"><span class="pshot__cue">View on GitHub</span></a></div><div class="project__hero-heading"><h1 class="project__title page-heading-reveal">Limeade</h1><p class="project__hero-sub">Real-time computer vision for scooter rider safety.</p><div class="project__hero-actions"><a class="project__hero-cta" href="https://github.com/Nizamohammed/Limeade" target="_blank" rel="noopener">View on GitHub</a></div></div></header><div class="project__meta project__meta--role"><span class="project__status"><span class="project__status-dot project__status-dot--done" aria-hidden="true"></span>Completed</span><span aria-hidden="true">·</span><span>Feb 2026</span><span aria-hidden="true">·</span><span>Hackathon, DemonHacks</span></div><p class="project__role"><span class="project__role-label">Role</span>Backend and ML engineer</p><section class="project__section"><p class="project__label">About</p><div class="project__body"><p>Limeade is a real-time computer vision system for scooter rider safety, built with my team at DemonHacks 2026. I trained the two YOLOv8 models that run in parallel to detect hazards and built the reasoning layer, a weighted danger score that routes urgent threats through an LLM into graded haptic and spoken alerts, while an optical-flow motion analyzer estimates how each one is approaching.</p></div></section><section class="project__section"><p class="project__label">Highlights</p><div class="project__body"><div class="project__group"><p class="project__group-title">Detection</p><ul class="project__list"><li>Dual YOLOv8 inference at about 5 FPS with an IoU-based multi-object tracker maintaining a 10-frame history per track.</li><li>Motion analyzer classifying detections across 9 directional regions and 5 distance buckets using Farneback optical flow.</li></ul></div><div class="project__group"><p class="project__group-title">Reasoning</p><ul class="project__list"><li>Weighted danger score combining distance (45%), approach rate (40%), and hazard count (15%), with a 3-consecutive-frame trigger threshold.</li><li>Asyncio WebSocket server forwarding structured threat data to an LLM reasoning layer for urgency-graded haptic and spoken rider alerts.</li></ul></div></div></section><section class="project__section"><p class="project__label">Stack</p><div class="project__body"><ul class="project__chips"><li class="project__chip">Python</li><li class="project__chip">YOLOv8</li><li class="project__chip">OpenCV</li><li class="project__chip">asyncio</li><li class="project__chip">WebSocket</li></ul></div></section><a href="/work" class="project__back project__back--bottom">← Work</a></article>
</BaseLayout>
